      "page_title": "Dead Tuples, Bloat, and VACUUM",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Exception: VACUUM truncates wholly-empty trailing pages",
            "That truncation grabs a brief ACCESS EXCLUSIVE lock",
            "VACUUM FULL blocks all reads and writes",
            "`pg_repack` / `pg_squeeze` compact online instead"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Two Maps"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Free Space Map (`fsm`): per-page free space, so INSERTs reuse room",
            "Visibility Map (`vm`): 2 bits per page — all-visible, all-frozen",
            "all-visible pages enable INDEX ONLY SCANs",
            "The executor then skips the heap fetch entirely"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Two-Pass Scan"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "scan heap",
              "collect dead tids",
              "clean every index",
              "free line pointers"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`maintenance_work_mem` sizes the dead-tid array",
            "Too small = repeated index passes over the same table",
            "PG17 replaced the array with a TID store",
            "Far less memory, far fewer repeat index scans"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Monitoring"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT relname, n_dead_tup, n_live_tup, last_autovacuum",
            "FROM pg_stat_user_tables ORDER BY n_dead_tup DESC;",
            "SELECT * FROM pg_stat_progress_vacuum;  -- stuck run",
            "SELECT * FROM pgstattuple('big_table');  -- exact, slow"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Reusable ≠ Returned",
          "text": "Plain VACUUM never shrinks the file. It only stops it from growing further."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Launcher Loop",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Launcher wakes every `autovacuum_naptime` (default 60s)",
            "It starts workers per database",
            "`autovacuum_max_workers` defaults to 3",
            "3 workers across hundreds of tables is a common bottleneck"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Trigger Formula"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "threshold = 50 + 0.2 * reltuples",
            "# vacuum_threshold + vacuum_scale_factor",
            "analyze  = 50 + 0.1 * reltuples"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
